<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalimullah Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1525–1527</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Kalim Allah Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalimullah Shah was the last sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>, a puppet of the Barid family at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a>. Around 1527 he fled the city and appealed for help to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a>, the new Mughal ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, and then to the sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar">Ahmadnagar</a>, but found no effective support and died in exile. His flight is taken as the end of the Bahmani dynasty.</p></div>
